# Cursor Rules Boundaries

- Shared project rules live in `.cursor/rules/` and are intended to be committed.
- Personal rules live in `.cursor/rules/local/` or use the `*.local.mdc` suffix.
- Do not edit, summarize, or rely on personal local rules unless the user explicitly asks.
- When adding shared rules, keep them concise and focused on project conventions.
- If a rule affects versioning, releases, or module boundaries, keep it consistent with `RELEASES.md`, module changelogs, and `gradle.properties`.
